statement: An assessment is not time-barred if it is issued after a departmental computation of the amount of tax with which a particular assessee is considered to be chargeable.
quote: Such rejection was possible only after a departmental computation of the amount of tax with which a particular assessee is considered to be chargeable.

### 24 draftly-rule-courts-coa-c.a.-dc_1043_1997.pdf-1  method=llm-extract statute='SRC029-s110'
text_path: data/processed/docs/case-law/courts/coa/c-a-dc-1043-1997-4c9ca64a50.md
statement: The burden of seeking and getting evidence before court, in the course of investigation of title to the land sought to be partitioned by parties before Court, prior to deciding what share should go to which party is more the duty of the judge than the contesting parties.
quote: The burden of seeking and getting evidence before court, in the course of investigation of title to the land sought to be partitioned by parties before Court, prior to deciding what share should go to which party is more the duty of the judge than the contesting parties.

### 25 draftly-rule-courts-coa-c.a.-dc_1086_1996-f-2.pdf-1  method=llm-extract statute=''
text_path: data/processed/docs/case-law/courts/coa/c-a-dc-1086-1996-f-2-a94633580c.md
statement: In a partition case, it is incumbent on the judge to investigate into the title of each party before he arrives at a determination.
quote: In a partition case, it is incumbent on the judge to investigate into the title of each party before he arrives at a determination [Chandrasena v. Piyasena and Others (1999) 3 SrLL.R. 201] and it would be the prime duty of the trial judge to carefully examine and investigate the actual rights and titles to the land sought to be partitioned [Sopinona v. Pitipanaarachchi and Two Others (2010) 1 SrLL.R. 87].

